Viewer: wireless music no longer stutters, and no crackle when it starts (2026-10-12).

On the F50 the iPhone's AAC packets came over Wi-Fi with a gap of about 400 ms in every 5 s window, then all
at once. The page cut the music into 20-frame (427 ms) fragments and played 0.65 s behind the newest audio,
so the element ran dry now and then and later skipped ahead. Starting playback (opening the page, a CarPlay
restart on going full screen) jumped to the very last sample, which ran dry at once: a crackle.
AAC now goes to the element 4 frames (85 ms) at a time and plays 1 s behind; starting playback leaves the
same margin. Wired FLAC keeps 0.65 s. Desktop Chrome, 20 s of AAC with a 400 ms gap every 3 s: the element
waited 3 times and skipped once before, waited only once at the start (no audio yet) and never skipped after.

